  "question": {
    "text": "If $f(x)=x\\left(\\frac{1}{x-1}+\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{x+1}\\right), x>1$. Then"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$f(x) \\leq 1$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$1     < f(x) \\leq 2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$2     < f(x) \\leq 3$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$f(x)>3$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given function is\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\nf(x) &=x\\left\\{\\frac{1}{x-1}+\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{x+1}\\right\\}, x>1 \\\\\r\n&=x\\left\\{\\frac{2 x}{x^{2}-1}+\\frac{1}{x}\\right\\}=\\frac{2 x^{2}}{x^{2}-1}+1 \\\\\r\n&=\\left\\{\\frac{2}{\\left(1-\\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\right)}+1\\right\\}>3\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad f(x)>3$"
  }
}